  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * @brief Q31 matrix multiplication
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcA points to the first input matrix structure
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcB points to the second input matrix structure
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * @param[out]      *pDst points to output matrix structure
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * @return     		The function returns either
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * <code>ARM_MATH_SIZE_MISMATCH</code> or <code>ARM_MATH_SUCCESS</code> based on the outcome of siz
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * @details
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * \par
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * The function is implemented using an internal 64-bit accumulator.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * The accumulator has a 2.62 format and maintains full precision of the intermediate
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * multiplication results but provides only a single guard bit. There is no saturation
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * on intermediate additions. Thus, if the accumulator overflows it wraps around and
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * distorts the result. The input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * overflows. The input is thus scaled down by log2(numColsA) bits
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * to avoid overflows, as a total of numColsA additions are performed internally.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * The 2.62 accumulator is right shifted by 31 bits and saturated to 1.31 format to yield the final
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  *
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * \par
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  * See <code>arm_mat_mult_fast_q31()</code> for a faster but less precise implementation of this fu
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  *
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/MatrixFunctions/arm_mat_mult_q31.c ****  */
